Below is the final, refined V2 blueprint for InfoGrid, based on everything we discussed: monetization potential, AI-resistance, security, DevOps relevance, and future V3 expansion.

The goal of V2 is important to understand first.

InfoGrid V2 — Purpose

V2 is the foundation platform.

It proves that InfoGrid can:

Aggregate knowledge from multiple repos

Render it cleanly as a platform

Support multi-user access

Maintain structure automatically

Prepare for enterprise features in V3

Think of V2 as the operating system of InfoGrid.

Not the full product yet.

Core Capabilities V2 Must Achieve

By the end of V2 the platform must be able to:

• Pull content from multiple repositories
• Organize them automatically
• Render a documentation platform
• Allow API access to knowledge
• Support CLI/Web consumption
• Maintain versioning
• Run secure CI/CD
• Prepare for client data later

